        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Classify Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777037371483"
          },
          "code": "CLASSIFY_INTENT",
          "id": "1777037075838",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777037075840_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Classify the user’s message into exactly ONE intent: RATE_INQUIRY | UPDATE_RATE_INQUIRY | NOT_SUPPORTED\n\nDefinitions:\n- RATE_INQUIRY:\n  The user is requesting a brand-new shipment rate or asking how to ship goods. This typically includes details such as item, ship unit count, origin, destination, weight, or volume. The request is self-contained and does not depend on a previous quote or prior shipment details.\n  Examples:\n  - \"How to ship 100 units from A to B\"\n  - \"Get me a rate for shipping item X from LA to NY\"\n\n- UPDATE_RATE_INQUIRY:\n  The user is referring to a previous rate inquiry or quote and wants to modify it, reuse it, or ask a what-if variation. This includes explicit edits and implicit follow-ups. Classify it as UPDATE_RATE_INQUIRY when the message implies \"same item\", \"same source\", \"same destination\", \"previous item\", \"use the prior quote\", \"that one\", \"this shipment\", \"what if\", \"instead\", \"now\", \"but\", \"change only\", or similar follow-up language. Or when the message implies to change any one or more parameters from the previous rate inquiry, such as item, location, ship unit count, weight, volume, perspective, and request type. If the user is building on an earlier rate inquiry in the conversation, treat it as an update even if the message does not contain words like \"update\" or \"change\".\n  Examples:\n  - \"Change destination to C\"\n  - \"Update weight to 200 lb\"\n  - \"Make it 150 units instead\"\n  - \"What if I ship the same item from A to B\"\n  - \"Same shipment, but change destination to A.\"\n  - \"Use previous item but quantity is now 1000.\"\n\n- NOT_SUPPORTED:\n  The request is unrelated, unclear, or outside the scope of rate inquiry or updates.\n  Examples:\n  - \"Track my shipment\"\n  - \"Cancel the order\"\n  - \"Change equipment group\"\n  - \"Hello\"\n\nRules:\n- If the message depends on prior rate context → UPDATE_RATE_INQUIRY\n- If the message is asking for a new rate and includes shipment details → RATE_INQUIRY\n- If unclear or unrelated → NOT_SUPPORTED\n- When in doubt, choose NOT_SUPPORTED\n\nOutput:\n- Return ONLY the intent label.\n- Do not include any explanation or extra text.\n\nUser message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
