        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Update Inquiry"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777041336384"
          },
          "code": "UPDATE_INQUIRY",
          "id": "1777040095989",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777040095990_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are updating a rate inquiry context based on a user’s message.\n\nCurrent structured context (source of truth):\n- itemName: {{$context.$variables.itemGid}}\n- shipUnitCount: {{$context.$variables.shipUnitCount}}\n- weight: {{$context.$variables.weight}}\n- weightUnit: {{$context.$variables.weightUnit}}\n- volume: {{$context.$variables.volume}}\n- volumeUnit: {{$context.$variables.volumeUnit}}\n- sourceLocationName: {{$context.$variables.sourceLocationGid}}\n- destLocationName: {{$context.$variables.destLocationGid}}\n- perspective: {{$context.$variables.perspective}}\n- requestType: {{$context.$variables.requestType}}\n\nRecent conversation (for resolving ambiguity only):\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} \n\nUser message:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\nTask:\n- Identify which fields the user is modifying.\n- Update ONLY those fields.\n- Keep all other existing values unchanged.\n- Return the FULL updated context.\n\nPriority rules (VERY IMPORTANT):\n1. Use explicit values from the current user message first.\n2. Use structured context as the source of truth for all unchanged fields.\n3. Use conversation history ONLY if the user message is ambiguous (e.g., \"it\", \"same\", \"previous\", \"make it cheaper\").\n4. Never override a valid existing value unless the user clearly requests a change.\n\nField definitions:\n- shipUnitCount: Number of ship units.\n- itemName: Item name. Always convert to UPPERCASE.\n- sourceLocationName: Origin location. Always convert to UPPERCASE.\n- destLocationName: Destination location. Always convert to UPPERCASE.\n- requestType:\n  - \"AllOptions\" → default or if user wants all options\n  - \"LowestCost\" → if user mentions cheapest, lowest cost\n  - \"FastestTransit\" → if user mentions fastest, quickest\n- perspective:\n  - \"B\" → default or buy rate\n  - \"S\" → if user explicitly requests sell rate\n- weight: Weight per ship unit.\n- weightUnit: Convert to UPPERCASE. Detect from user input. Possible values: LB, KG, KIP, TON, MTON, CAR, HK, KG P.\n- volume: Volume per ship unit.\n- volumeUnit: Convert to UPPERCASE. Detect from user input. Possible values: CUFT, CUIN, CUYD, CUMTR, GALCAN, GALUS, L, DMQ, BBL, BBLLARGE, PROOF GA, PERCENT ALCOHOL, PROOF L, L PURE ALCOHOL, CMQ, ML.\n\nGuidelines:\n- Use context to interpret synonyms:\n  - \"kilos\", \"kg\" → KG\n  - \"cubic meters\" → CUMTR\n  - \"liters\" → L\n- If user updates a field, overwrite it.\n- If user does NOT mention a field, keep existing value.\n- If ambiguous and cannot be resolved even with history, do NOT update that field.\n- Do NOT remove valid existing values unless explicitly changed.\n\nOutput:\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object in this format:\n{\n  \"itemName\": \"<string>\",\n  \"shipUnitCount\": <number>,\n  \"sourceLocationName\": \"<string>\",\n  \"destLocationName\": \"<string>\",\n  \"weight\": <number>,\n  \"weightUnit\": \"<string>\",\n  \"volume\": <number>,\n  \"volumeUnit\": \"<string>\",\n  \"perspective\": \"<string>\",\n  \"requestType\": \"<string>\"\n}"
